# Delete Method Implementation Pattern

When implementing delete functionality in repositories and services, follow this consistent pattern demonstrated in [ingredient.repository.ts](mdc:src/modules/ingredient/repositories/ingredient.repository.ts) and [ingredient.service.ts](mdc:src/modules/ingredient/services/ingredient.service.ts).

## Repository Pattern

```typescript
async delete(id: string): Promise<boolean> {
  const result = await this.repository.delete(id);
  return result.affected > 0;
}
```

### Key Points:

- Use TypeORM's `delete()` method with entity ID
- Return boolean based on `result.affected > 0`
- Method name should be `delete`, not `remove`

## Service Pattern

```typescript
async delete(id: string): Promise<boolean> {
  const deleted = await this.repository.delete(id);
  if (!deleted) throw new NotFoundException('Entity not found message');
  return deleted;
}
```

### Key Points:

- Call repository's `delete` method directly
- Throw `NotFoundException` (or appropriate exception) if deletion failed
- Return the boolean result from repository
- Don't pre-check if entity exists - let the delete operation determine success

